add(4,'One robot, independent moving agents','Singapore',35,
'The controlled robot must reach its goal without access to the true future of other agents.','simulation-video',{'type':'simulation-video'},
['**One** robot chooses the avoidance motion','**Independent** agents disturb the path','**Success = safe arrival**'],
"This simulation illustrates the task: one controlled robot and independent moving agents. The agents did not coordinate their avoidance with my robot. My rover had to reach a goal while avoiding fixed obstacles, moving agents, and the arena boundary. It could use their current observed positions, but not their true future motion. I evaluated both arrival and clearance, because staying still can look safe while completely failing the task.",
"Those requirements shaped the limits and assumptions of the system.",[
 d('Independent agents','Did all robots cooperate?','No. Only the controlled rover performed avoidance. The agents received their own commands before the run.',['Their realized paths could drift.','The experiment is not coordinated multi-robot planning.'],img('multi-agent-poster.jpg','Physical robots; one controlled rover'),'P A B',locator='Draft §3.1.4'),
 d('Robot geometry','How was the robot represented?','The campaign uses a conservative circular envelope of radius 0.130 m.',['A disc simplifies distance calculations.','It is an envelope, not the exact chassis outline.'],eq('d = ‖x − c‖ − r_agent − r_robot\nr_robot = 0.130 m','Campaign geometry / draft Eq. (1)'),'P COST A',locator='Draft §2.1; Table 1'),
 d('Clearance','Does negative clearance mean contact?','It means the modeled safety discs overlap. It does not by itself establish physical contact.',['Zero means envelope contact.','Measured position uncertainty also matters.'],table(['Clearance','Meaning'],[['d > 0','Separated envelopes'],['d = 0','Touching envelopes'],['d < 0','Overlapping envelopes']]),'P COST',locator='Draft §2.1 and §3.7.2'),
 d('Goal and success','How did you define success?','I combined no collision, no arena exit and no execution error with arrival inside the goal tolerance.',['The physical stopping tolerance is 0.08 m.','Final stopping distance is not ultimate positioning accuracy.'],eq('I_joint = I_safe × I_goal\nI_goal = 1 when ‖x − x_goal‖ ≤ 0.08 m','Physical success definition'),'P A B',locator='Draft Eq. (2)–(4), (32)')])

